From 26dfb717c90cc09d960357bc5f98da71caad997b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jose M. Caballero Guerrero"
 <80172778+Caballero-git@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:24:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/30] arm64: dts: rockchip: P25T: enable tsadc SoC thermal
 sensor

The RK3568 has an on-die temperature sensor (tsadc) already fully wired
in rk356x-base.dtsi, including a thermal-zones node with CPU and GPU
zones and trip points - it's just status = "disabled" by default,
same shape as &gpu and &i2s1_8ch were before their own enable patches.

hw-tshut-mode/polarity copied verbatim from two independent reference
boards using this SoC (rk3566-quartz64-a.dts, rk3568-qnap-tsx33.dtsi),
which agree on the same values - this is SoC-internal thermal-shutdown
wiring, not board-schematic dependent like the RK817 audio pins were.

No kernel .config change needed (CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_THERMAL and
CONFIG_THERMAL_HWMON were already enabled) and no RK817 involvement -
DTB-only change. Once booted, temperatures are available directly via
/sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone*/temp or through the standard `sensors`
command (lm-sensors package, no sensors-detect probing needed/used).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0156c5MfQpFxaYWNNLMrcym9
---
 .../boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
index ff6777cfd..7444fd3ae 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
@@ -633,3 +633,23 @@ &i2s1_8ch {
 	rockchip,trcm-sync-tx-only;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * SoC thermal sensor (patch 0016). Disabled by default in
+ * rk356x-base.dtsi, same shape as &gpu/&i2s1_8ch above - but here the
+ * thermal-zones node (cpu_thermal using <&tsadc 0>, a gpu thermal zone
+ * using <&tsadc 1>, both with trip points) already exists too, so
+ * nothing else needs wiring. hw-tshut-mode/polarity copied verbatim
+ * from two independent real reference boards that agree on the same
+ * values for this exact SoC - rk3566-quartz64-a.dts and
+ * rk3568-qnap-tsx33.dtsi - this is SoC-internal thermal-shutdown
+ * wiring, not board-schematic dependent like the RK817 audio pins
+ * were, so no board-specific verification needed. No RK817/kernel
+ * .config changes required (CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_THERMAL and
+ * CONFIG_THERMAL_HWMON are already enabled) - DTB-only change.
+ */
+&tsadc {
+	rockchip,hw-tshut-mode = <1>; /* tshut via GPIO, not CRU */
+	rockchip,hw-tshut-polarity = <0>; /* GPIO active-low */
+	status = "okay";
+};
